      'Setup example: 12 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: In positive contracts, declarer's side wins by taking at least 36 of 70 card points. Various contracts have different objectives (avoid tricks, win exact number of tricks, etc.).",
      "Turn-flow example: Point-trick game with bidding. Players bid contracts; highest bidder becomes declarer. In many contracts declarer calls a king to choose a secret partner. Declarer may exchange cards with the six-card talon. After announcements (bonuses, kontras), forehand leads to the first trick. Players must follow suit if possible, otherwise must play a trump. In positive contracts declarer's side needs at least 36 of 70 card points to win; negative contracts have different objectives (e.g. lose every trick in Bettel).",
      "Scoring example: Card points determine if contract is made. Game points and bonuses determine payments. In positive contracts declarer's side wins by taking at least 36 of 70 card points. In negative contracts (e.g. Bettel, Piccolo) objective is to lose every trick or win exactly one or two tricks. Game points and bonuses determine payments..",
